Indeed keyboard keys never converted to inp.x/y. That's a bug. Need add keyboard vector update each frame or in keydown/up. Easiest in E.update before updatePlayer: compute keyboard axes if no joystick. But joystick sets x/y. Need distinguish joystick active. Could add `r.input.joyActive` flag. Simpler: in keydown/up, after updating keys, recompute x/y from keys unless joystick pointer active. Joystick handlers set input.x/y directly; keyboard events won't interfere except while moving with joystick and pressing keyboard. We can maintain `r.input.keyboard` flag. Implement `syncKeyboardVector()` called keydown/keyup:

```
function syncKeyboardVector() {
  if (r.input.joyActive) return;
  const k=r.input.keys;
  let x=(k.d||k.arrowright?1:0)-(k.a||k.arrowleft?1:0);
  let y=(k.s||k.arrowdown?1:0)-(k.w||k.arrowup?1:0);
  const len=Math.hypot(x,y)||1;
  r.input.x=x/len; r.input.y=y/len;
}
